      "notes": "Policy-compliant four-B70 single-session DeepSeek V4 Flash K160 repeatability repair. The fused KV insertion previously issued overlapping BF16 and RoPE stores; vLLM 93fde4186 makes their write regions disjoint. Consecutive testing then localized deterministic graph-prefill corruption to large oneCCL SYCL all-reduces. An exact-version oneCCL 2021.17.2 build routes only all-reduces above 128 KiB through the safe path while keeping decode collectives fast. Ten independent exact captures pass 10/10. Two strict cold suites reached 40.170350 and 40.096205 tok/s median, every prompt cached_tokens=0. All four worker maps loaded the selected hashed libccl and matching SYCL/UR runtime. No speculation, prefix cache, history, or response reuse. K160 remains an experimental hash-pruned performance artifact. The older 40.135724 row is retained as historical speed evidence but is not the repeatability authority."
